{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_08a480bc2930b2bacc5f48274268e8d41191e6f71dbb6395f12a4bd76888f3c9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: local development uses git clone followed by cargo run to build and execute the agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0e735734f6479d252b30488b3007fa0a1c0b7d751afcf8c10b3b4e5bcdb2ec7e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Recipes defined in picocode.yaml support inline prompts or prompt files, and can pin a persona and model per recipe."},{"claim_ids":["clm_18badee181a23da5e332ec19866d246bd71de86391e684ed570e54de5c23ae22"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Destructive actions such as deleting files or running shell commands require manual confirmation by default; --yolo disables all confirmation prompts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_339d94fddef2798179b7138dac787df0f71c0bd853e7a20c14aec774c7d069e6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: hacking on picocode requires Rust (latest stable) and a provider API key; new tools are added in src/tools.rs with #[rig_tool] and registered in src/agent.rs's build_rig_agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4cebaceae44e5ebbfa28efaa6ec0feb6e0c486656b60527d47542cc9d3730792"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Multi-provider LLM support (Anthropic, OpenAI, DeepSeek, Google, Ollama, and others) is provided via the Rig library."},{"claim_ids":["clm_85b57fc66a9f15f3cffbe78022bf4a393fc52ac1691966376af82f4addeadc08"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users can switch expert personas (e.g., architect, security, zen) via --persona to change how the agent thinks and speaks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a5c5965e9cab445f0f34d1af726a622b4877421aad113580c00ea30293b7a0da"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"picocode is described as a minimal, high-performance coding agent written in Rust, shipped as a single compact binary."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ac74669940cd19dc0fe52b71e454f476efa55f547458bcd81f84d77eaca4b4b4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A local AGENTS.md file can supply the agent with custom codebase-specific instructions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ccbff68f23d69cb924e9c2661ef1d47b1ad94efea05c2799241e888ad5b0ede0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent exposes filesystem tools (read/write/edit/list/make/remove/move/copy), grep_text, glob_files, a bash tool, and an optional agent_browser for web automation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cf4ccd84e5b8029ef451eea565288dbdd3f5538911aa5175799dff445ec5da41"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The crate is structured as a library plus binary; library users call create_agent with an AgentConfig specifying provider, model, output, yolo, and tool_call_limit."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ea3725fcde65690257189cc63760e826c55b9130447ef9fd300a87e89b01e48f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Flags include --provider, --model, --yolo to disable confirmations, --quiet for piping, --persona, and --tool-call-limit with a default of 50."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ff4b68fea7d08de4c3dbe45305fd54160235a4d74249f488c3e5b373a6dc3b5b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers interactive chat (default), single-prompt mode, and a recipe subcommand that runs named tasks from picocode.yaml."}],"claim_ids":["clm_08a480bc2930b2bacc5f48274268e8d41191e6f71dbb6395f12a4bd76888f3c9","clm_0e735734f6479d252b30488b3007fa0a1c0b7d751afcf8c10b3b4e5bcdb2ec7e","clm_18badee181a23da5e332ec19866d246bd71de86391e684ed570e54de5c23ae22","clm_339d94fddef2798179b7138dac787df0f71c0bd853e7a20c14aec774c7d069e6","clm_4cebaceae44e5ebbfa28efaa6ec0feb6e0c486656b60527d47542cc9d3730792","clm_85b57fc66a9f15f3cffbe78022bf4a393fc52ac1691966376af82f4addeadc08","clm_a5c5965e9cab445f0f34d1af726a622b4877421aad113580c00ea30293b7a0da","clm_ac74669940cd19dc0fe52b71e454f476efa55f547458bcd81f84d77eaca4b4b4","clm_ccbff68f23d69cb924e9c2661ef1d47b1ad94efea05c2799241e888ad5b0ede0","clm_cf4ccd84e5b8029ef451eea565288dbdd3f5538911aa5175799dff445ec5da41","clm_ea3725fcde65690257189cc63760e826c55b9130447ef9fd300a87e89b01e48f","clm_ff4b68fea7d08de4c3dbe45305fd54160235a4d74249f488c3e5b373a6dc3b5b